WEBVTT

00:01.000 --> 00:02.000
["Lazarus" playing]

00:02.120 --> 00:05.680
♪ Look up here I'm in heaven ♪

00:09.200 --> 00:13.040
♪ I've got scars that can't be seen ♪

00:16.280 --> 00:20.240
♪ I've got drama, can't be stolen ♪

00:23.840 --> 00:27.200
♪ Everybody knows me now ♪

00:36.080 --> 00:37.560
He was in the war.

00:39.320 --> 00:41.920
He was in a tunnel collapse.

00:42.000 --> 00:43.640
[exhaling]

00:43.720 --> 00:44.880
He won medals.

00:48.440 --> 00:49.920
Take care of him.

01:01.080 --> 01:04.760
♪ Look up here, man, I'm in danger ♪

01:08.240 --> 01:11.640
♪ I've got nothing left to lose ♪

01:14.880 --> 01:19.160
♪ I'm so high, it makes my brain whirl ♪

01:22.800 --> 01:26.360
♪ Dropped my cell phone down below ♪

01:40.400 --> 01:41.440
[door opens]

01:42.720 --> 01:44.600
[nurse] Here he is, Mr. Shelby.

01:47.160 --> 01:48.320
[Michael] Thank you, nurse.

01:51.000 --> 01:52.080
Tommy.

01:58.640 --> 02:01.240
I need to speak to you about the priest.

02:01.320 --> 02:02.560
[breathing heavily]

02:05.520 --> 02:07.080
I know things about him.

02:07.160 --> 02:08.160
Hmm.

02:10.680 --> 02:12.600
From when I was a…

02:12.680 --> 02:14.000
From when I was a boy.

02:22.240 --> 02:24.880
I will shoot him myself, Tommy.

02:27.000 --> 02:28.680
Just teach me how to shoot.

02:30.720 --> 02:31.720
[scoffs]

02:32.640 --> 02:34.160
It's easy, Michael.

02:36.000 --> 02:36.960
Just point.

02:38.040 --> 02:39.280
Pull the trigger.

02:52.040 --> 02:53.520
[door opens]

03:01.720 --> 03:02.800
[infant cooing]

03:31.960 --> 03:32.960
[exhales]

03:52.040 --> 03:55.120
[door opens and closes]

03:56.360 --> 03:57.520
[footsteps approaching]

04:08.760 --> 04:11.280
He asked for me today, Mary.

04:13.680 --> 04:15.000
Not his mother.

04:16.680 --> 04:17.920
For the first time.

04:19.240 --> 04:20.279
He missed you.

04:21.360 --> 04:23.280
Where is he? Is he in the kitchen?

04:23.360 --> 04:25.200
Yes, he's with the girls and Johnny.

04:25.280 --> 04:26.280
[clears throat]

04:31.160 --> 04:33.000
Did you remember your medicine, sir?

04:35.960 --> 04:37.960
Do you ever read the Bible, Mary?

04:39.440 --> 04:40.720
Sometimes.

04:40.800 --> 04:44.440
Do you ever read it out loud
while standing naked next to my bed?

04:47.240 --> 04:49.880
'Cause when I take the morphine
the doctor gave me,

04:49.960 --> 04:51.800
that's what you do.

04:51.880 --> 04:53.360
I'm wide awake,

04:54.280 --> 04:57.400
but you are standing there naked,
plain as day,

04:58.520 --> 05:00.520
reading from the Book of Leviticus.

05:03.040 --> 05:04.560
Do you wanna know what happens next?

05:08.000 --> 05:09.080
No.

05:10.280 --> 05:11.440
Neither do I.

05:12.960 --> 05:14.880
That's why I poured the medicine away.

05:17.040 --> 05:18.280
Go and get Johnny, Mary.

05:26.360 --> 05:28.920
-[imperceptible yelling]
-[electric guitar playing]

05:50.000 --> 05:51.880
-[imperceptible]
-[sniffles]

05:53.040 --> 05:55.400
Without the firing pins,
the guns won't work.

05:55.480 --> 05:56.840
And there are no replacements?

05:56.920 --> 06:00.400
They don't make these anymore.
These are the end of the line.

06:01.160 --> 06:03.320
Yeah, we had the foreman take out
all the spares.

06:03.400 --> 06:05.920
Take the pins, they'll never fire a shot.

06:06.000 --> 06:10.520
Nobody will know until they unload
the bloody things in Tbilisi.

06:10.600 --> 06:12.960
Or until they are facing our guns
at Kutaisi.

06:13.040 --> 06:14.800
Take them all out and give them to me.

06:14.880 --> 06:16.680
Oh, come on, boys, no fucking about.

06:16.760 --> 06:18.320
And I will tell the Soviet Ambassador

06:18.400 --> 06:20.480
that there is no longer a need
to blow up the train.

06:20.560 --> 06:22.480
[Arthur]
I will tell Tommy you accept his plan.

06:23.480 --> 06:24.480
[spits]

06:28.240 --> 06:30.440
[Johnny]
You know, some mornings I wake up,

06:30.520 --> 06:34.360
I think I've died and this is heaven, Tom.
[chuckles]

06:34.440 --> 06:39.080
I mean, the wives and kids camped out
by the valley, huh, not being moved on.

06:39.160 --> 06:45.240
Sure, me and myself. I'm surrounded
by maids and food and booze. [chuckles]

06:47.160 --> 06:48.560
See that line there?

06:51.320 --> 06:52.360
No.

06:53.240 --> 06:54.600
It's the edge of heaven.

06:57.160 --> 06:59.880
The border
between Birmingham and paradise.

07:01.880 --> 07:08.160
And today, my friend, you are gonna
step over that line back into the world.

07:09.480 --> 07:11.960
You mean you have something
for me to do, Tom.

07:13.960 --> 07:16.960
Have you ever heard
of Hampton Court Palace, Johnny?

07:17.600 --> 07:19.840
No. I can't say I have.

07:19.920 --> 07:22.800
You and three families of the Lees
are gonna set up camp

07:22.880 --> 07:25.600
100 yards from the gate of the Palace.

07:25.680 --> 07:28.360
You won't be moved on
because I have just bought the land.

07:28.440 --> 07:30.720
You'll be joined
by some old friends of mine

07:30.800 --> 07:33.880
who are gonna open a hole
underneath your tents and caravans.

07:35.720 --> 07:37.600
You see this blow to the head
you took, Tom…

07:37.680 --> 07:41.200
And for allowing the hole to be dug,
you will get ₤5,000,

07:41.280 --> 07:43.840
which you will split between
the three Lee families.

07:46.240 --> 07:49.680
I take a lot of this money is to do with
not asking questions, Tommy?

07:52.520 --> 07:53.560
Dead right, Johnny.

07:53.640 --> 07:57.880
And when the hole is filled in again,
you can go back to paradise.

08:01.680 --> 08:02.680
[sighs]

08:02.760 --> 08:05.520
[Mary] Mr. Shelby, your brothers are here.

08:06.800 --> 08:10.080
And there is someone who described himself
as the "Wandering Jew."

08:12.400 --> 08:13.520
[groans slowly]

08:14.640 --> 08:17.360
Will you take the Jewish gentleman
to the drawing room?

08:20.080 --> 08:23.400
Take my brothers to the kitchen
and give them tea and rum. [clears throat]

08:23.480 --> 08:24.320
[Mary] Yes, sir.

08:24.400 --> 08:25.520
[door opens]

08:35.480 --> 08:37.039
Good morning, Mr. Solomons.

08:37.960 --> 08:39.039
Yeah, it is.

08:42.080 --> 08:44.200
Nice little place you've got here, Thomas.

08:45.280 --> 08:46.280
What is it?

08:46.360 --> 08:50.040
A foreclosure of a gambling debt
from some poor young lord

08:50.120 --> 08:53.600
who you pumped full of opium
in one of your casinos?

08:53.680 --> 08:56.040
Or is that just tittle-tattle?

08:56.120 --> 08:57.240
Drink?

08:57.320 --> 08:58.760
Nah, I don't touch it, mate.

08:58.840 --> 09:01.880
Your housekeeper said
you're not allowed to drink.

09:02.840 --> 09:03.720
Eh?

09:04.800 --> 09:11.080
She said you are suffering from so many
ancient injuries from your sporting life

09:11.160 --> 09:14.200
that your head is like
some sort of smashed vase

09:14.280 --> 09:16.520
what has been stuck back together
by a horse.

09:20.160 --> 09:21.640
Now.

09:21.720 --> 09:24.080
Word in London is that you can be found

09:24.160 --> 09:27.880
wandering the streets of Birmingham
stark naked, throwing away money.

09:27.960 --> 09:30.480
You talk to dead people.

09:30.560 --> 09:34.160
Also, that you believe
that you are powerful enough

09:35.080 --> 09:39.440
to summon up Jews…

09:41.560 --> 09:43.800
of a very particular standing

09:43.920 --> 09:46.680
up to the gentile wilderness
wherein you live

09:46.760 --> 09:49.600
in order for them
to do your fucking bidding, mate.

09:50.480 --> 09:51.880
And still you came.

09:51.960 --> 09:54.320
Yeah, well, you know,
I was passing, wasn't I?

09:58.880 --> 10:03.840
Do you know something, Alfie,
this morning I tried to read the paper,

10:03.920 --> 10:09.440
and I realized that the only consequence
of my terrible accident

10:09.520 --> 10:11.400
is that I now need glasses.

10:15.600 --> 10:16.520
Right.

10:20.040 --> 10:23.520
Right. Well, I know a man…

10:25.520 --> 10:27.640
who can make you a pair of these.

10:28.200 --> 10:30.480
He is a magician, mate.

10:30.560 --> 10:31.960
He is a magician.

10:33.040 --> 10:36.800
So not only will you be able
to read your newspaper…

10:38.960 --> 10:43.080
but you will also be able to see
into the future.

10:45.400 --> 10:49.920
Now, I know this, right,
because he made this pair here for me.

10:51.680 --> 10:55.000
So you don't have to worry
about telling me what this is all about,

10:55.080 --> 10:58.000
because I have already seen it.

11:07.160 --> 11:10.160
You're fucking about with Russians,
isn't you, you silly boy?

11:11.400 --> 11:13.280
You've got two choices, Michael.

11:13.920 --> 11:17.160
You fuck off to America with Arthur,
join the Apaches,

11:17.240 --> 11:19.920
-or you marry the girl.
-This isn't a joke.

11:20.000 --> 11:23.080
Arthur, are you really gonna live
with the Apaches?

11:23.160 --> 11:25.720
-Told her father yet?
-No.

11:25.800 --> 11:28.520
He'll fucking shoot you, man.
Are you sure the kid's yours?

11:28.600 --> 11:30.400
[Michael sighs] I wish I hadn't told you.

11:30.480 --> 11:33.840
Then think of marriage
as a beautiful road,

11:33.920 --> 11:35.800
flowers all the way down it.

11:35.880 --> 11:38.640
-Is he joking?
-Oh, it's hard to tell these days.

11:41.880 --> 11:43.040
Do you, uh…

11:44.040 --> 11:45.160
Do you love the woman?

11:47.800 --> 11:48.800
Fucking what?

11:48.880 --> 11:51.080
Go and marry her like the rest of us.

11:51.160 --> 11:53.080
She doesn't want her family to know.

11:53.160 --> 11:54.680
She doesn't wanna have the baby.

11:54.760 --> 11:56.880
-We know a woman.
-Shut up, John.

11:56.960 --> 11:58.440
Same woman who helped you out twice.

11:58.520 --> 11:59.640
-Not my women.
-Mmm-hmm?

12:00.560 --> 12:02.080
That's why you had them fixed, Arthur.

12:02.640 --> 12:03.960
Charlotte will want the best.

12:04.040 --> 12:05.560
-[John] She is the best.
-The best?

12:05.640 --> 12:08.280
She used to be a nurse. 20minutes. Done.

12:08.360 --> 12:11.240
You don't have to go to in
or wait outside.

12:11.320 --> 12:15.120
You go to The Garrison,
drink whiskey, have a laugh.

12:15.200 --> 12:16.200
Remember, John?

12:17.240 --> 12:21.200
Then this kid walks in, no shoes on,
says, "It's done."

12:21.760 --> 12:24.440
Second time we was in there, same kid.

12:24.520 --> 12:28.160
This time he's wearing… shiny new shoes.

12:30.280 --> 12:33.360
-He shouts, "It's done, Arthur."
-And what?

12:36.800 --> 12:41.720
She bought new shoes…
with the money I gave her.

12:44.000 --> 12:45.960
It was for a good cause.

12:46.040 --> 12:47.040
[Johnny] Arthur?

12:47.120 --> 12:49.320
If you're gonna get on like this
with the Apaches,

12:49.400 --> 12:50.760
they'll fucking scalp you, boy.

12:50.840 --> 12:52.000
[bell ringing]

12:53.360 --> 12:56.600
Tommy said when that bell rings
we're to all go to the big room.

13:02.520 --> 13:04.440
Come on. Tommy has a plan.

13:22.200 --> 13:24.200
-Arthur!
-[inhales sharply]

13:24.320 --> 13:26.080
-Arthur?
-[Tommy] Arthur, come here.

13:28.000 --> 13:29.440
-[Alfie] Shalom!
-[groans]

13:30.720 --> 13:33.160
Arthur, shalom.

13:33.240 --> 13:35.240
-Alfie.
-Shalom.

13:35.800 --> 13:37.400
Come here. Come. Let's sit down.

13:37.480 --> 13:41.440
I owe you a little something, don't I?
I do. Come on.

13:41.520 --> 13:44.400
Sit down. Come on, sit down here.

13:44.960 --> 13:46.800
[grunting] There you go.

13:46.880 --> 13:47.880
Right.

13:49.600 --> 13:50.960
Listen.

13:51.040 --> 13:52.120
Arthur.

13:53.200 --> 14:00.120
I want you to know that whatever happened
between us back then, that was business.

14:01.200 --> 14:03.080
It was just business. All right?

14:04.080 --> 14:11.040
And I also want you to know that I have
made my apologies via my own God

14:11.120 --> 14:18.080
for abusing a very holy day to get you
clinked up and battered, which I did.

14:18.160 --> 14:24.120
And now I would also like to extend
my personal apologies unto you.

14:33.200 --> 14:34.040
All right?

14:37.240 --> 14:40.680
I hear that you have allowed Jesus
to come into your life.

14:40.760 --> 14:41.760
Eh?

14:42.480 --> 14:43.760
Oh, you heard then.

14:43.840 --> 14:47.320
Yeah, that's beautiful, that's wonderful.
That is lovely, isn't it?

14:47.400 --> 14:48.400
That is lovely.

14:49.560 --> 14:53.040
And I was wondering, how does that
work for you on a day to day

14:53.120 --> 14:54.960
considering your line of work, mate?

14:59.840 --> 15:01.320
Your apology is accepted.

15:04.720 --> 15:06.880
'Cause I hear
you're a right fucking nuisance with it.

15:06.960 --> 15:08.600
-[chuckles]
-[inhales sharply]

15:10.080 --> 15:11.240
Hello…

15:12.720 --> 15:14.600
You see, all I am saying is that

15:14.680 --> 15:17.280
every man, he craves certainty,
doesn't he?

15:17.360 --> 15:22.680
He craves a certainty
even if that certainty of yours, right…

15:22.760 --> 15:24.080
Well, I mean…

15:25.360 --> 15:27.840
It's fucking fanciful mate, isn't it?

15:27.920 --> 15:28.920
[seething]

15:29.880 --> 15:30.880
Eh?

15:43.200 --> 15:46.800
I'm Old Testament.

15:48.960 --> 15:51.120
Fucking hell. Look at that. Now, that…

15:52.920 --> 15:55.000
That scares me more.

15:55.920 --> 15:58.880
Yeah. Congratulations, Tommy.

15:58.960 --> 16:02.200
You now have the finished article
right here, don't you?

16:02.280 --> 16:07.840
See, that man, right, he will murder
and maim for you with God on his side.

16:09.240 --> 16:10.280
Yeah.

16:13.920 --> 16:15.680
You don't wanna let him go.

16:17.120 --> 16:21.880
If we're gonna do business
with this fucker, I demand to know why.

16:26.440 --> 16:28.160
[Tommy] Right. [sighs]

16:28.240 --> 16:32.680
While I was in the hospital,
I formulated a plan,

16:35.880 --> 16:37.560
and this is how it's gonna work.

16:38.440 --> 16:41.040
So, the Russians
cannot be trusted to pay us.

16:42.280 --> 16:44.320
We are gonna take what is ours.

16:45.680 --> 16:47.720
We need to see what's in their treasury.

16:49.040 --> 16:52.000
And that is why we need Mr. Solomons.

16:52.080 --> 16:53.080
["Cherry Lips" playing]

17:13.720 --> 17:16.599
[sighs] All right, boys, just remember

17:17.680 --> 17:19.440
they're fucking insane.

17:20.520 --> 17:23.760
And dangerous
and drunk on stuff we've never heard of.

17:24.720 --> 17:27.160
And they're worse than us
for spirits and ghosts.

17:30.800 --> 17:33.400
Today they're gonna test us.

17:35.400 --> 17:36.480
Fuck them.

17:44.360 --> 17:46.640
[Arthur] The Russians all turned and ran.

17:48.000 --> 17:49.760
The Cossacks didn't run, Arthur.

18:02.520 --> 18:04.320
Mr. Shelby, welcome.

18:05.160 --> 18:07.320
-How's my car?
-I think I'm in love with it.

18:08.200 --> 18:10.040
And I yours.

18:10.120 --> 18:11.920
So we should keep what we love, yes?

18:12.000 --> 18:16.320
Excuse the reception. Whenever we open
the treasury, the Cossacks are on guard.

18:21.760 --> 18:22.760
[spits]

18:25.040 --> 18:30.680
[Tommy] In Russia, men on the other side
of the law decorate their body in tattoos.

18:30.760 --> 18:32.000
-Nice.
-Right.

18:32.080 --> 18:38.000
Now, some of these tattoos are proof of
allegiance to underground organizations,

18:38.080 --> 18:40.880
which are the sworn enemies
of the royal household.

18:41.000 --> 18:47.280
So, it's customary
in Russian royal households

18:47.360 --> 18:50.440
to check for such tattoos
before engaging a man in business.

18:51.080 --> 18:53.760
And as we approach the allotted day,
these ladies here

18:53.840 --> 18:57.720
would like to make sure that
you're not assassins or infiltrators…

18:57.800 --> 18:58.840
No, we are all good.

18:58.920 --> 19:00.520
So they would like to check your skin.

19:03.000 --> 19:06.040
-They wanna check our skin?
-Yeah.

19:06.120 --> 19:07.960
Now, my body's already been checked.

19:08.040 --> 19:11.680
Although at the time,
I wasn't sure that was the reason.

19:11.760 --> 19:12.920
And now it's your turn.

19:14.520 --> 19:17.320
Come on, boys. Take your clothes off.

19:17.880 --> 19:19.160
[scoffs]

19:19.240 --> 19:20.440
Fuck off.

19:20.520 --> 19:22.720
No, no, no.

19:22.800 --> 19:23.800
Obey.

19:24.800 --> 19:25.840
I see.

19:25.920 --> 19:27.280
Obey, Arthur.

19:28.800 --> 19:30.920
No, I won't be obeying nobody.

19:31.000 --> 19:32.600
Get out of my way, both of you.

19:32.680 --> 19:33.760
Arthur, come here.

19:35.360 --> 19:37.440
[in Romany]
I told you they're all fucking mad.

19:37.520 --> 19:39.440
They're only half joking.

19:41.320 --> 19:45.160
Let the ladies have their fun.

19:45.240 --> 19:46.800
Eh? Eh?

19:51.320 --> 19:53.640
[John speaking English]
Come on, Arthur. [chuckling]

19:53.720 --> 19:55.440
-[Arthur] Shut up, John.
-[John laughs]

19:55.520 --> 19:57.120
[Tatiana laughs]

19:57.200 --> 20:00.720
I will have a maid gather the buttons
and sew them back on.

20:03.280 --> 20:06.360
[in Russian] Remember he is the most
dangerous. The other one the prettiest.

20:16.360 --> 20:17.360
All right.

20:18.480 --> 20:19.720
Fuck it.

20:19.800 --> 20:20.920
There you go, ladies.

20:21.000 --> 20:24.080
-Made in fucking Birmingham.
-[John laughs]

20:25.920 --> 20:28.240
All right, I think
we have seen enough, eh?

20:29.920 --> 20:30.920
Tatiana.

20:34.760 --> 20:35.760
[John snickers]

20:36.400 --> 20:39.280
Your face, Arthur, is a fucking picture.

20:39.360 --> 20:42.760
Sometimes assassins hide their allegiances
behind their balls.

20:42.840 --> 20:44.520
[breathes deeply]

20:44.600 --> 20:46.160
[John continues snickering]

20:49.600 --> 20:51.440
But you pass the test, soldier.

20:53.280 --> 20:54.560
With flying colors.

21:00.360 --> 21:02.080
-[John chuckles]
-[moans softly]

21:06.800 --> 21:07.960
You see.

21:09.400 --> 21:10.640
[breathing heavily]

21:10.720 --> 21:12.160
He wants to be a good man.

21:21.080 --> 21:22.200
But there now.

21:23.520 --> 21:24.520
There.

21:28.120 --> 21:30.320
Inside every man there is a devil.

21:38.680 --> 21:39.680
[moans softly]

21:49.320 --> 21:51.840
-They're real diamonds, eh?
-[Tatiana sighs]

21:51.920 --> 21:56.800
[Izabella] It is traditional to
seal the successful examination

21:56.880 --> 21:58.840
with vodka and music.

22:01.080 --> 22:02.600
[John laughing]

22:05.000 --> 22:07.680
Holy fuck, Tom. What was that?

22:07.760 --> 22:09.760
Well done, boys. Eh?

22:10.400 --> 22:11.560
Well done, Arthur.

22:14.320 --> 22:16.200
Now you know what we have to do next.

22:17.080 --> 22:18.080
All right?

22:19.000 --> 22:20.000
One last job.

22:20.560 --> 22:23.480
Make contact and play nice.

22:33.840 --> 22:35.120
Another five minutes.

22:38.880 --> 22:42.840
I brought Michael because as
chief accountant he has to be witness.

22:42.920 --> 22:44.560
Ada, can I, uh, use your phone?

22:44.640 --> 22:45.760
Michael.

22:47.800 --> 22:49.040
Business first.

23:06.440 --> 23:08.320
Michael, stop looking at your watch.

23:11.760 --> 23:15.080
Ada, whilst you are reading this, um,
can I go and use your phone?

23:16.120 --> 23:17.760
Who is the lucky girl, Michael?

23:17.840 --> 23:20.520
Her name is Charlotte,
and Michael cannot breathe

23:20.600 --> 23:22.960
if he does not talk to her
every two hours.

23:23.040 --> 23:24.280
Ada, please.

23:25.520 --> 23:26.520
Phone's in the hall.

23:26.600 --> 23:28.400
-Dial naught for the line.
-Thank you.

23:28.480 --> 23:30.200
And keep it quick, I pay the bill.

23:30.280 --> 23:32.480
-I will.
-Not for long.

23:32.560 --> 23:33.560
[Ada chuckles]

23:35.480 --> 23:37.600
[breathing deeply]

23:51.400 --> 23:54.800
Think about it, Pol.
Together we can take control.

23:54.880 --> 23:57.640
